b.com/users/Ashutosh0x/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashutosh0x/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashutosh0x/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashutosh0x/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashutosh0x/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashutosh0x","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Opened #46248 for this. Your analysis pinned it exactly — I just turned `bwd_recv_id` into a disjunction over every element of `back_pairs` instead of `back_pairs.back().second`.\n\nWorth noting for reviewers that `ForwardCycleMultipleCycles` asserted the buggy shape (a single `constant(1)` and one compare), so the existing test encoded the behaviour rather than catching it; that expectation is updated in the PR. The single-cycle tests are untouched, since with one back edge the loop runs once and emits identical HLO.\n\nI wasn't able to build XLA locally, so it rests on CI.","created_at":"2026-07-27T06:21:52Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/45222#issuecomment-5087974484","id":5087974484,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/45222","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABL0RUVA","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5087974484/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-07-27T06:21:52Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5087974484","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161562995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashutosh0x/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashutosh0x/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashutosh0x/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https: